3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">It&#x27;s xAI&#x27;s image-to-video preview model - and it&#x27;s available to run right here. You give it one starting image plus a prompt, and it animates that exact frame into cinematic video: camera moves, atmosphere, physics, and sound direction, all while keeping the look and lighting of your original.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">How do I use it here?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Upload one source image as your start frame, write a prompt describing the motion, pick your settings, and generate - no API keys or code needed. We handle the model; you just bring the frame and the idea.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What do I need to get started?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Just two things: a single starting image and a prompt describing how it should move. Drop in your frame, describe the shot, and generate.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">How should I write a prompt for the best result?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Describe what moves and how - the camera move, the pacing, the atmosphere, and the sound you want. Be specific about direction (&quot;slow push-in,&quot; &quot;pan left,&quot; &quot;embers drifting&quot;) rather than just naming objects. The clearer the motion, the closer the result.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">When should I keep a prompt short?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">When you want the model to fill in natural motion and you&#x27;re exploring quickly. Less direction gives it more room to interpret - good for fast tests and simple animations.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">When should I use a detailed prompt?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">When you have a specific shot in mind. Spell out the camera move, timing, and mood together - for example: &quot;Slow cinematic push-in as embers drift across the scene and the fabric stirs in the wind.&quot; More detail means more control.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">How do I get clear subject motion?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Anchor the prompt to what should move and in what direction. Name the subject&#x27;s action explicitly instead of leaving it implied, so the model knows what to animate and what to hold steady.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What if I don&#x27;t specify every detail?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">The model fills in the rest from your frame and prompt. It keeps the detail and lighting of your input, so even a light prompt stays faithful to your original - you just hand over more of the creative choices.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">What settings can I choose?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Resolution at 480p or 720p, and clip length anywhere from 2 to 15 seconds. Set them per generation to match where you&#x27;re publishing.</div></details><details class="landing-faq-item group border-b border-divider-primary pt-2"><summary class="flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-5 py-4 text-lg font-semibold transition hover:text-font-secondary active:text-font-disabled [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden list-none"><span class="text-left">Can I make longer scenes?</span><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" class="size-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M3.81344 7.97848C4.0087 7.78322 4.32528 7.78322 4.52055 7.97848L10.0003 13.4583L15.4801 7.97848C15.6754 7.78322 15.9919 7.78322 16.1872 7.97848C16.3825 8.17374 16.3825 8.49032 16.1872 8.68558L10.3539 14.5189L10.0003 14.8725L9.64677 14.5189L3.81344 8.68558C3.61818 8.49032 3.61818 8.17374 3.81344 7.97848Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></summary><div class="pb-4 text-sm text-font-secondary whitespace-pre-line">Yes. Generate each shot, then chain them into longer sequences that keep a consistent look across the whole project.</div></details></section></div><section class="py-10 md:py-20 container max-w-8xl relative"><div aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"></div><h2 class="text-brand-h-sm font-bold text-center mb-8 uppercase font-grotesk md:text-brand-h-lg">Explore more AI features</h2><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 justify-center"><a href="/cinematic-video-generator" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-grid items-center text-font-secondary bg-surface-primary font-medium px-3">Cinema Studio</a><a href="/ai/video" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-grid items-center text-font-secondary bg-surface-primary font-medium px-3">Visual Effects</a><a href="/ai/image?model=soul" class="h-8 rounded-full md:rounded-lg inline-grid items-center text-font-secondary bg-surface-primary font-medium px-3">Higgsfield Soul</a><a href="/ai/video?model=kling-v